/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  swro01_campoDalias -- THE PLOT PLAN, UP TO THE FENCE (DEV.md 4c C194).

  THIS IS CHOUPO'S DESIGN OF A PLANT OF THIS SCALE, NOT THE REAL SITE'S PLAN.
  The case study the flowsheet is built on (Toray, MC-CS-CAMPODEDALIAS-1910)
  gives no site plan, no coordinates and no building sizes.  Every position,
  footprint, road, the rack, the fence opening and every crossing below is an
  AUTHOR-SET ASSUMPTION FOR THIS EXERCISE, round numbers chosen so that the
  checks are visible; none is taken from the real plant, a spacing table or
  a code (Choupo ships none).  The engine's own contributions are the sizes
  the sizing pass published (the tanks' volumes, the exchanger array's count)
  and the checks.

  THE SITE.  The sea is to the SOUTH.  The intake pipeline arrives at the
  south fence and the brine outfall leaves it there; the process runs
  south -> north: intake pumps and pretreatment (a row along the south), the
  reverse-osmosis building (the pump hall along its south wall, the first-pass
  hall, the second-pass hall north of it and the energy-recovery hall at its
  east end), and the product stores in the north, from where the product leaves by the north
  fence.  The administration (offices, control room, laboratory, workshop) is
  west, along the entrance road from the gate on the north.

  WHERE THE PLAN STOPS (Vitor's decision, C194): AT THE FENCE.  The
  crossings below name what lies beyond -- the 1.6 km subsea intake pipeline,
  the brine outfall and its diffuser, the irrigation and potable network --
  and none of it is drawn.

  THE PLANT IS SIX TRAINS IN ONE BUILDING (DEV.md 4c C199, C272).  The sizing
  pass yields one item per train for each high-pressure pump, booster,
  second-pass pump, energy-recovery array and vessel bank (`HPpump/train1` ..
  `RO2b/train6`: 42 items).  TRAIN 1 IS DECLARED IN FULL (its seven items
  below) and the other five are a REPEAT of it, declared once in `typicals`:
  the engine moves train 1's items by the pitch, sizes each from its own
  sizing, stands it in its room and checks and pipes it like any item; the
  plan and the 3D draw trains 2..6 as outlines, "typical of train 1".  The
  vessel banks publish their own envelope (the racks side by side, the loading
  clearance at the east end), so they declare no footprint here; the pumps and
  arrays publish none, so their plan boxes are author-set.  All 42 stand in
  the rooms of the `building {}` at the end of this file (pump hall,
  first-pass hall, second-pass hall, energy-recovery hall), which fixes their
  base on the floor and makes the engine refuse an item that does not fit its
  room; a room lists train 1's item and the repeats follow.  Train k stands at
  x = -100 + 19 (k - 1) m (its energy-recovery array at y = -27 + 5 (k - 1) m).
  The pretreatment is still a pair of NON-PROCESS boxes.

  WHAT THE PIPE ROUTER CAN AND CANNOT DO HERE.  Indoor piping is not routed
  (the building's rooms and service voids are not drawn), and the router
  draws one line per STREAM, to the first train's item: the six trains' lines
  are identical.  The three lines that leave the building (the spent brine to
  the outfall, the two second-pass permeates to the product junction) are
  DECLARED below, from their wall penetration; the rest of the indoor streams
  are listed as not routed with their reason.  The pretreatment's streams are
  not routed either (the filters are placeholders with no sized item).  The
  intake line is routed to the fence through a one-inlet `mixer` (the intake
  chamber), the only way a stream whose first unit has no sizer reaches it.
  THE RUN ANNOUNCES SIX FINDINGS and leaves them: the five water tanks have no
  bund (a civil matter this exercise does not declare) and the site has one
  entrance.
  Footprints of the tanks are SQUARE boxes of the diameter their volume needs
  at the declared height (V = pi D^2 H / 4, cylinder-equivalent), declared
  because the storage sizer publishes a volume and no diameter.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

